<title>USA: Haarmann &amp; Reimer settles with Justice Dept.</title>
<headline>Haarmann &amp; Reimer settles with Justice Dept.</headline>
<dateline>SPRINGFIELD, N.J. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Haarmann &amp; Reimer Corp said Wednesday it had pleaded guilty to anti-competition charges and agreed to pay $50 million over five years.</p>
<p>The company said the charges arose from allegations that its Food Ingredients Division, along with several other companies, engaged in anti-competitive activities in the sale of citric acid.</p>
<p>It pleaded guilty after reaching an agreement with the U.S. Department of Justice to settle the charges, it said.</p>
</text>
